From: Ignacio Soriano <isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 16] i915: execbuffer throttling without a struct file on illumos

eb_pin_timeline() reads eb->file->filp->f_flags to decide whether the wait
for an older request of the same context (eb_throttle()) may block. The
facade's struct drm_file has no struct file on illumos (filp is NULL, see
include/drm/drm_file.h), so an execbuffer on a context that still has a
request in flight dereferences NULL: BAD TRAP type=e addr=0x2c in
eb_pin_timeline+0x105, on a Haswell GT3e (8086:0d22, iMac14,1) with the
headless i915n, in a loop of EXECBUFFER2 on the render ring. On illumos
the wait is that of a blocking file and stays interruptible.

License: the hunk is a trivial preprocessor guard on a MIT Linux file;
this patch is applied to the pinned Linux tree, not part of illumos-drm's
sources.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gem/i915_gem_execbuffer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gem/i915_gem_execbuffer.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gem/i915_gem_execbuffer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gem/i915_gem_execbuffer.c
@@ -2524,7 +2524,15 @@
 	intel_context_timeline_unlock(tl);
 
 	if (rq) {
+#ifdef __illumos__
+		/*
+		 * The facade's drm_file has no struct file (filp is NULL):
+		 * wait as on a blocking file, interruptibly.
+		 */
+		bool nonblock = false;
+#else
 		bool nonblock = eb->file->filp->f_flags & O_NONBLOCK;
+#endif
 		long timeout = nonblock ? 0 : MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT;
 
 		if (i915_request_wait(rq, I915_WAIT_INTERRUPTIBLE,
